    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d431-a1">

                <pb facs="0853" n="729" sameAs="frus:frus1881/pg729"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 1 in No. 1385.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Bingham to Mr.
                            Inouye.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Tokei</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1881-10-14"><hi rendition="#italic">October</hi> 14,
                        1881</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Dear Sir</hi>: I beg most heartily to congratulate
                    you upon the imperial decree of His Majesty the Emperor of Japan, of date the
                    12th instant, declaring his purpose to establish an imperial parliament. What
                    His Majesty has resolved to do accords with all the great reforms he has already
                    inaugurated, of which I made mention in my dispatch to my government, No. 1159,
                    as published in the <ref target="frus:frus1880/pg_690">Foreign Relations for
                        1880, page 690</ref>, a copy of which I gave you.</p>
                <p>To hasten slowly in this crowning work, at His Majesty proposes, is the dictate
                    of wisdom.</p>
                <p>I am, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>JNO. A. BINGHAM.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
